description = [=[mod id 3426836832

[h1]Blast to the Past (B2TP)[/h1]

[b]TL;DR:[/b] a vanilla-flavored balance mod for 6v6-8v8 Natural Selection 2, the original size public servers ran at. Most changes either tweak some values or mechanics to what vanilla used to run years ago, or incorporate changes from CompMod or good ideas from CBM, with the goal of improving skill expression while still remaining valuable for a managed, coordinated public server experience.

[hr][/hr]

[h1]ALIENS[/h1]

[h2]Skulk[/h2]
[list]
[*][b]Leap energy[/b] 45 -> 55 [i](CompMod value)[/i]
[*][b]Vampirism[/b] 4.66% -> 3.77% per shell [i](CompMod value)[/i]. Vampirism also works on Exos now
[/list]

[h2]Gorge[/h2]
[list]
[*][b]Gorges can drop tunnels themselves[/b] 5 Pres per entrance [i](adapted from CompMod, whose own drop cost is 4)[/i], but only into a room with no working power node [i](unbuilt, destroyed or damaged)[/i], or onto infestation. They come up fully mature and spread infestation immediately
[/list]

[h2]Lerk[/h2]
[list]
[*][b]Lerk health[/b] 180 -> 170 [i](CompMod value)[/i]
[*][b]Lerk spike damage[/b] 5 -> 5.5 [i](interpolated from CompMod, whose own value is 6)[/i]
[/list]

[h2]Fade[/h2]
[list]
[*][b]Advanced Swipe[/b] new at Biomass 8 -- +8% swipe damage [i](CompMod's own damage scalar, exactly)[/i], 30 Tres, 90 second research [i](CompMod's own cost/research time are 25 Tres / 60s -- tuned for B2TP)[/i]. This will kill a marine on armor 2 in three swipes. Countered by armor 3
[*][b]Stab energy[/b] 30 -> 25
[*][b]Stab research[/b] 25 -> 20 Tres
[/list]

[h2]Onos[/h2]
[list]
[*][b]Boneshield HP[/b] 1000 -> 600 [i](1000 was balanced for 10v10)[/i]
[*][b]Stomp energy[/b] 30 -> 45 [i](curbs stomp spam when the alien team has no adrenaline or a shift to sustain it)[/i]
[*][b]Stomp[/b] (CBM change) now slows marines caught in it instead of knocking them down -- same slow as being webbed, tapering off over 5 seconds
[/list]

[h2]Upgrades[/h2]
[list]
[*][b]Aura[/b] no longer reveals health
[/list]

[h2]Chamber hive passives[/h2]
Inspired by the CBM changes, but conditioned to be available only while the matching Hive is still alive.
[list]
[*][b]Shells[/b] regenerate themselves out of combat as long as the aliens have a Crag hive
[*][b]Veils[/b] cloak themselves out of combat as long as the aliens have a Shade hive
[*][b]Spurs[/b] can be picked up and moved by the commander as long as the aliens have a Shift hive
[/list]

[h2]Cysts[/h2]
[list]
[*][b]Build time[/b] 3.33 -> 6 seconds [i](CompMod value)[/i]
[*][b]Shift hive build multiplier[/b] x1.25 -> x1.5 [i](CompMod value)[/i], since vanilla cysting is broken in normal player counts
[*][b]Flame damage[/b] split by source [i](CompMod value)[/i]: welders x5 -> x4, flamethrowers x5 -> x7
[*][b]Mature cyst health[/b] 400 -> 300
[*][b]Detection range[/b] 8m -> 10m [i](CompMod value)[/i]
[*][b]Drifters[/b] ordered onto an unbuilt cyst now queue up the whole chain behind it, instead of one cyst at a time
[/list]

[h2]Tunnels[/h2]
[list]
[*][b]Relocating[/b] 6 -> 5 Tres [i](CompMod value)[/i]
[*][b]Minimap[/b] tunnel entrances are now labelled Entry 1-4 and Exit 1-4 on the map
[/list]

[h2]Hallucinations[/h2]
[list]
[*][b]Biomass health[/b] removed -- hallucinations no longer get tougher as biomass rises [i](CompMod change)[/i]
[*][b]Abilities[/b] hallucinated Lerks can no longer use Umbra or Spores [i](CompMod change)[/i]; hallucinated Onos can no longer Stomp [i](B2TP's own extension of the same idea)[/i]
[/list]

[hr][/hr]

[h1]MARINES[/h1]

[h2]Round start[/h2]
Marines start with 1 IP (vanilla!) but
[list]
[*][b]7v7[/b] +5 Tres
[*][b]8v8[/b] +10 Tres
[/list]
This serves as an interpolation between 1 IP and no bonuses for 6v6 (vanilla behavior) and +1 IP for the arcade clusterfugg that is 10v10, which is essentially +20 Tres. The only way to give "half an IP" is to give Tres. Giving a straight IP for 8v8 amounts to nonstop early marine pressure and can snowball easily into marines choking out the aliens.

[h2]Structures and units[/h2]
[list]
[*][b]ARC health[/b] 2600 -> 2100 [i](interpolated -- CompMod's own value is 1800)[/i]
[*][b]ARC armor[/b] 400 -> 500 [i](CompMod value)[/i], limited to 4 [i](CompMod value)[/i]
[*][b]MAC speed[/b] +15% out of combat [i](CompMod value)[/i]
[*][b]MAC rollout speed[/b] 2 -> 5 [i](CBM fix)[/i]
[*][b]Sentry[/b] 5 -> 6 Tres [i](CompMod value)[/i]
[*][b]Sentry Battery[/b] 10 -> 12 Tres [i](CompMod value)[/i]
[/list]

[h2]Drops[/h2]
[list]
[*][b]Welder drop[/b] 3 -> 2 Tres
[*][b]Mine drop[/b] 7 -> 5 Tres
[*][b]Dropped weapon stay time[/b] 16 -> 20 seconds
[/list]

[h2]Medpack Tech[/h2]
Marines get Medpack Tech #1 and #2, ported from ENSL CompMod seasons 13 and 14:
[list]
[*][b]Default[/b] heal 25/25, identical to vanilla
[*][b]Medtech #1[/b] unlocks in the command station, requires armory. Heal 30/20
[*][b]Medtech #2[/b] unlocks in the command station, requires AA and Medtech #1. Heal 40/10
[/list]
This makes medding scale as the round progresses, since vanilla meds are truly lacking in the end game.

[h2]Weapons[/h2]
[list]
[*][b]Weapon upgrade scaling[/b] 7.84% (?!) -> 10% per level, for all weapons including shotgun, FT and GL [i](a W3 shotgun meatshot goes from 210 to 221 damage)[/i]
[*][b]Shotgun falloff start[/b] 5m -> 7.5m
[*][b]Shotgun falloff end[/b] 15m -> 17.5m
[/list]
The shotgun change is half of the CompMod change (CompMod moves falloff to 10m/20m; B2TP splits the difference with vanilla's 5m/15m). The 50% damage floor past the falloff-end range is unchanged vanilla/CompMod behavior -- only where the falloff starts and ends has moved. Vanilla shotguns aren't terrible now. There's a reason the 10v10 meta skips them over entirely for AA.

[hr][/hr]

[h1]Credits[/h1]

[b]Author:[/b] Bleu

[b]Developed for:[/b] the NS2 Sudamerica community. Join us at [url=https://discord.gg/NS2-Sudamerica]discord.gg/NS2-Sudamerica[/url].

Several changes here are ported or adapted from ENSL CompMod / CBM, with permission from their respective authors.]=]
